Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] File cache: evict the least recently used file when the 64 slots run out

Fixes the preview.31-rc1 OLED crash (EU, GPU renderer, second battle, in the
battle report): requestFile (engine/file/file_cache.c) took the slot from
findFreeFileSlot, which returns NULL when all 64 slots are used, and wrote
slot->file through NULL+4 (SIGSEGV, far=0x4, in STFGTREP_drawReport ->
getFileEntry -> loadFile -> waitForFile -> requestFile). US has the same code
and the same bug.

Cause: on the PS1 the heap is 1.33 MB (0x800AA800..0x801FF000), and allocMem /
allocMemHigh call FILE_CACHE.evictOldest() until an allocation fits, so memory
pressure kept the cache small and 64 slots never filled (had they, the NULL
write would have hit kernel RAM). The host heap is 8 MiB (host_heap.c), so
nothing evicts and a session of a couple of hours fills every slot.

Policy: when no slot is free, requestFile does what allocMem does when the
heap is full: evictOldestFile() frees the loaded file used least recently
(findOldestFile: biggest on a tie), then the request takes that slot. This is
the game's own eviction path, so every file it can evict is one the PS1 would
also evict under heap pressure, and the game already tolerates it:
- only FILE_LOADED slots are candidates, so a queued or reading file (its
  buffer is the CD reader's target) is never freed;
- the game protects what it needs by touching it: isFileLoading, requestFile,
  loadFile and updateFileCache refresh lastUsed, getFileEntry reaches loadFile
  every frame it draws, and markCachedFiles / touchMarkedFiles refresh the
  files cached before a field load. The oldest candidate is therefore a file
  nothing touched for the longest time, never one used this frame while an
  older one exists.
If no loaded file exists (every slot queued or reading, which the loaders'
synchronous waits make impossible), dw3_port_file_cache_fatal logs it through
psyz (dw3.log) and aborts, so the crash report names the cause instead of a
NULL write. Each eviction is logged (the first 16, then every 256th) as
`dw3-file-cache: all 64 slots taken, evicted the least recently used file ...`.
PS1 builds (PORT_HOST off) are untouched.

Tested with the DW3_FILE_CACHE_SLOTS hook of 0095 on US and EU
(replay scenarios us/eu-file-cache-full).

--- a/src/engine/file/file_cache.c
+++ b/src/engine/file/file_cache.c
@@ -112,6 +112,22 @@
         return;
     }
     slot = findFreeFileSlot();
+#if PORT_HOST
+    if (slot == NULL) {
+        /* Every slot is taken. The original never got here: the heap was small enough that
+           allocMem evicted files long before 64 were cached. Do what allocMem does when the heap
+           is full: free the loaded file used least recently (the queued and the reading ones are
+           never candidates, so nothing in use by the cache is lost), then take its slot. */
+        FileSlot *old = findOldestFile();
+
+        if (old == NULL) {
+            dw3_port_file_cache_fatal(file, FILE_CACHE_SLOTS);
+        }
+        dw3_port_file_cache_evicted(file, old->file, FILE_CACHE_SLOTS);
+        evictOldestFile();
+        slot = findFreeFileSlot();
+    }
+#endif
     slot->file = file;
     slot->data = HEAP.alloc(FILE_TABLE.getSectorCount(file) * CD_SECTOR_SIZE, MEM_FILE_CACHE);
     slot->state = FILE_QUEUED;
